1
00:00:06,042 --> 00:00:09,041
<i>Two people have been
found dead at a motel in Sinaloa.</i>

2
00:00:09,042 --> 00:00:11,291
<i>Last night, forces clashed</i>

3
00:00:11,292 --> 00:00:13,958
<i>as a military operation
confronted cartel members.</i>

4
00:00:21,292 --> 00:00:23,624
<i>Police have successfully
captured and arrested</i>

5
00:00:23,625 --> 00:00:26,583
<i>three local cartel members,
all suspected to have been involved...</i>

6
00:00:27,750 --> 00:00:30,041
<i>of the crimes
attributed to Iván Gastélum,</i>

7
00:00:30,042 --> 00:00:32,874
<i>who might better be known
as his alias, El Cholo.</i>

8
00:00:32,875 --> 00:00:36,457
<i>Deployed the military
all across the country.</i>

9
00:00:36,458 --> 00:00:37,624
<i>The deployment signals...</i>

10
00:00:37,625 --> 00:00:40,916
<i>A tribute was held
to honor all of the brave men and women</i>

11
00:00:40,917 --> 00:00:43,624
<i>who have lost their lives
in the line of duty.</i>

12
00:00:43,625 --> 00:00:46,332
<i>We will always remember their sacrifices.</i>

13
00:00:46,333 --> 00:00:50,041
<i>The military seek to strike
a devastating blow to the cartel</i>

14
00:00:50,042 --> 00:00:52,082
<i>with the loss of one of their leaders.</i>

15
00:00:52,083 --> 00:00:54,000
I know it's about to be a bloodbath.

16
00:01:01,958 --> 00:01:05,458
{\an8}BASED ON AN ARTICLE BY
HÉCTOR DE MAULEÓN

17
00:01:06,208 --> 00:01:08,707
<i>Requesting any additional units
in the area.</i>

18
00:01:08,708 --> 00:01:10,917
<i>-Unit Two, en route.
-Unit Six, en route.</i>

19
00:01:15,333 --> 00:01:18,332
{\an8}Put both hands on the table right now!
Hey. Don't be an idiot.

20
00:01:18,333 --> 00:01:19,667
<i>Don't be an idiot.</i>

21
00:01:33,917 --> 00:01:37,124
FACING EL CHAPO

22
00:01:37,125 --> 00:01:39,875
BASED ON TRUE EVENTS

23
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:49,167
{\an8}JANUARY 6TH, 20167:00 AM
LOS MOCHIS, SINALOA

24
00:01:56,083 --> 00:01:57,292
Stop it!

25
00:01:59,625 --> 00:02:00,625
Elízabeth!

26
00:02:01,250 --> 00:02:04,082
Elízabeth! Don't ignore me
when I talk to you.

27
00:02:04,083 --> 00:02:05,916
Stop it now, okay?

28
00:02:05,917 --> 00:02:08,557
-Here's your uniform and coffee, honey.
-You're the best. Thanks.

29
00:02:08,958 --> 00:02:11,457
How come you don't buy them
more appropriate toys?

30
00:02:11,458 --> 00:02:12,791
Like Barneys or Barbies.

31
00:02:12,792 --> 00:02:14,791
I would never buy them
those ridiculous toys.

32
00:02:14,792 --> 00:02:16,666
It's from Carlitos, Papa.

33
00:02:16,667 --> 00:02:18,332
Course it was. Give me a break.

34
00:02:18,333 --> 00:02:20,999
Hey! Enough!
Will you stop shooting and sit?!

35
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:22,582
Listen to your dad.

36
00:02:22,583 --> 00:02:25,791
-Eat all your eggs and beans, okay?
-When are you going to buy us a computer?

37
00:02:25,792 --> 00:02:29,249
Mom said we might actually quiet down
because it would keep us busy.

38
00:02:29,250 --> 00:02:30,583
Jeez.

39
00:02:32,750 --> 00:02:35,624
Do you want me to take this one?

40
00:02:35,625 --> 00:02:38,166
You remember everything, Joana?
And what did I tell you?

41
00:02:38,167 --> 00:02:40,832
That your papa will buy you a computer
as soon as he can.

42
00:02:40,833 --> 00:02:44,291
Let me ask you two something.
Do you guys think you deserve a computer?

43
00:02:44,292 --> 00:02:47,166
You keep bothering your sister.
And you, have you done your homework?

44
00:02:47,167 --> 00:02:48,332
Yes!

45
00:02:48,333 --> 00:02:50,582
-What do you mean, "yes"?
-Well, no.

46
00:02:50,583 --> 00:02:52,332
Mm.

47
00:02:52,333 --> 00:02:55,582
But, Dad, I get good grades
and I never ask for anything.

48
00:02:55,583 --> 00:02:57,041
-Well...
-Morning!

49
00:02:57,042 --> 00:02:58,582
Okay, I'll think about it.

50
00:02:58,583 --> 00:03:02,416
-Come on in. Do you want a coffee, or...
-We don't have time. We're late!

51
00:03:02,417 --> 00:03:04,457
Okay, come on, girls.
This is what you get,

52
00:03:04,458 --> 00:03:07,041
'cause you guys kept fooling around
and ran out of time!

53
00:03:07,042 --> 00:03:09,082
-Listen to your mom.
-See you later, Arturo.

54
00:03:09,083 --> 00:03:10,916
Let's go! Run, run, run!

55
00:03:10,917 --> 00:03:12,874
Sorry, sweetie. May God be with you.

56
00:03:12,875 --> 00:03:15,082
-We're blessed! We have to go.
-Bye.

57
00:03:15,083 --> 00:03:16,875
-Bye!
-Thanks for helping us out.

58
00:03:23,333 --> 00:03:25,499
Hey, Liz is a little troublemaker, huh?

59
00:03:25,500 --> 00:03:27,832
We need to watch what we say
because she's getting clever.

60
00:03:27,833 --> 00:03:29,167
-Yeah, I know.
-Mm-hmm.

61
00:03:29,833 --> 00:03:31,250
Come eat. Aren't you hungry?

62
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:33,167
No appetite.

63
00:03:36,292 --> 00:03:37,750
Are you feeling okay?

64
00:03:38,667 --> 00:03:40,750
No. To be honest, I haven't been great.

65
00:03:46,375 --> 00:03:47,833
What's wrong, honey?

66
00:03:48,583 --> 00:03:51,333
Is it your head? Your stomach?
What's bothering you?

67
00:03:54,125 --> 00:03:55,250
I'm pregnant.

68
00:04:04,333 --> 00:04:05,792
I'm pregnant, Arturo.

69
00:04:11,917 --> 00:04:15,458
-You're not joking, are you?
-And why would I joke about this?

70
00:04:18,708 --> 00:04:20,208
Another daughter?

71
00:04:20,708 --> 00:04:21,874
Or maybe a son?

72
00:04:21,875 --> 00:04:23,458
Holy shit.

73
00:04:26,125 --> 00:04:28,083
I thought you were taking the pill.

74
00:04:33,542 --> 00:04:35,416
Of course I was, Arturo.

75
00:04:35,417 --> 00:04:37,917
I just forgot a couple of days.
That's all.

76
00:04:46,083 --> 00:04:47,707
I looked at our budget again,

77
00:04:47,708 --> 00:04:50,875
and with my salary, we should be fine.

78
00:04:53,333 --> 00:04:56,582
We're paying for the house, though.
We're paying for the car.

79
00:04:56,583 --> 00:05:00,417
Not to mention all the girls' needs.
Sweetheart, we're barely staying afloat.

80
00:05:01,333 --> 00:05:02,333
-I just...
-Well...

81
00:05:03,875 --> 00:05:05,707
We won't keep it if it's too much trouble.

82
00:05:05,708 --> 00:05:08,042
But that's not what I want us to do.

83
00:05:08,542 --> 00:05:11,124
I just want to be on the same page,
'cause we're having the baby.

84
00:05:11,125 --> 00:05:13,166
I'll go to Valladares
and ask for the night shift.

85
00:05:13,167 --> 00:05:16,999
Not the night shift, Arturo.
It's way more dangerous, honey.

86
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:18,457
Then what the hell do I do?

87
00:05:18,458 --> 00:05:21,374
Yes, the night shift will be a bitch,
but I'll get used to it.

88
00:05:21,375 --> 00:05:23,833
But what we can't get used to
is not eating.

89
00:05:26,458 --> 00:05:29,250
Well, I'd rather be poor than a widow. Hm?

90
00:05:31,750 --> 00:05:33,792
Oh, sweetheart.

91
00:05:38,417 --> 00:05:40,624
Good morning, sir.
Do you have two minutes?

92
00:05:40,625 --> 00:05:42,375
Close the door behind you.

93
00:05:43,750 --> 00:05:44,792
Everything good?

94
00:05:46,583 --> 00:05:49,874
Would it be possible for me
to move over to the night shift?

95
00:05:49,875 --> 00:05:53,250
No can do.
I need you out there during the day.

96
00:05:55,625 --> 00:06:00,875
It's just, well, because you can make more
on the night shift, and, um...

97
00:06:04,792 --> 00:06:06,582
Well, I'm going to be a dad again,

98
00:06:06,583 --> 00:06:08,833
and you know
the expenses that come with that.

99
00:06:09,333 --> 00:06:10,792
You guys are pregnant?

100
00:06:11,917 --> 00:06:12,917
Yeah.

101
00:06:18,292 --> 00:06:19,625
<i>Hey, what's up, girl?</i>

102
00:06:20,375 --> 00:06:22,667
I just picked up
the baby clothes from Vicky.

103
00:06:24,333 --> 00:06:25,375
Are you okay?

104
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:28,249
Yeah, don't worry. I'm fine.

105
00:06:28,250 --> 00:06:30,792
I can hold onto these
if you haven't told your husband yet.

106
00:06:33,333 --> 00:06:34,500
I broke the news today.

107
00:06:36,417 --> 00:06:37,417
And how'd it go?

108
00:06:38,542 --> 00:06:40,542
Well, he told me
we'll figure something out.

109
00:06:41,292 --> 00:06:42,833
He wants the night shift, but

110
00:06:43,667 --> 00:06:45,625
it's been dangerous lately, you know?

111
00:06:47,375 --> 00:06:53,207
FEDERAL POLICE

112
00:06:53,208 --> 00:06:54,375
Carmona.

113
00:06:55,333 --> 00:06:56,791
Yes, Commissioner.

114
00:06:56,792 --> 00:06:59,957
I've just been told we're having
an officer transfer from Arteaga.

115
00:06:59,958 --> 00:07:02,417
-Nuevo León?
-Michoacán.

116
00:07:02,917 --> 00:07:06,125
-It's been a little crazy over there, no?
-So you heard that too.

117
00:07:06,625 --> 00:07:09,707
His last name is Rosales.
I put him on the night shift

118
00:07:09,708 --> 00:07:12,750
and I wasn't sure
which patrol to assign him to, but now...

119
00:07:13,750 --> 00:07:16,541
-Timing worked out perfectly, didn't it?
-Sure.

120
00:07:16,542 --> 00:07:18,832
That baby must be
a lucky charm for you, Arturo.

121
00:07:18,833 --> 00:07:21,375
Well, I'll need it.

122
00:07:21,958 --> 00:07:23,625
Hey, listen, Arturo.

123
00:07:24,125 --> 00:07:27,374
Make sure you watch this guy closely.
We don't know what he's like.

124
00:07:27,375 --> 00:07:28,832
Of course. I'll keep an eye on him.

125
00:07:28,833 --> 00:07:32,916
Good. Okay. I hope you're ready
for your double shift tonight.

126
00:07:32,917 --> 00:07:34,250
-Thanks again.
-Sure.

127
00:07:35,583 --> 00:07:38,582
So, do you like to ride
with a saddle or bareback?

128
00:07:38,583 --> 00:07:39,999
I hate saddles.

129
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:42,832
-Ha. So, bareback?
-Yes.

130
00:07:42,833 --> 00:07:44,041
Me too.

131
00:07:44,042 --> 00:07:45,832
-Here you go.
-Thank you.

132
00:07:45,833 --> 00:07:48,041
-See you next time.
-Thanks, Sandra!

133
00:07:48,042 --> 00:07:50,833
-Andrea.
-Oh, right, Andrea!

134
00:07:58,750 --> 00:08:00,625
Wait, I have to go now. Bye.

135
00:08:01,125 --> 00:08:03,208
Only way to get through a shift
is strong-ass coffee.

136
00:08:04,708 --> 00:08:05,708
Hm.

137
00:08:06,875 --> 00:08:11,207
We got a long night of driving around
and sitting on our asses.

138
00:08:11,208 --> 00:08:13,291
Is that all you think we do here?

139
00:08:13,292 --> 00:08:14,416
Chill out. Jesus.

140
00:08:14,417 --> 00:08:16,333
-Look, I'm just trying to fit in.
-Hmm.

141
00:08:24,792 --> 00:08:26,750
So, this coffee's strong to you?

142
00:08:29,208 --> 00:08:31,082
Come on. We just got started.

143
00:08:31,083 --> 00:08:33,707
<i>After forensics,
report to Unit 1 to get...</i>

144
00:08:33,708 --> 00:08:35,708
Well, welcome to Mochis.

145
00:08:37,708 --> 00:08:38,958
There you go.

146
00:09:04,167 --> 00:09:05,416
Check it out.

147
00:09:05,417 --> 00:09:07,457
He's fucked if he's not careful.

148
00:09:07,458 --> 00:09:10,375
Nah. He has everything under control.

149
00:09:12,750 --> 00:09:14,125
No, hey, wait!

150
00:09:14,958 --> 00:09:16,583
Man, what the fuck?

151
00:09:35,667 --> 00:09:36,667
Good evening.

152
00:09:37,167 --> 00:09:38,167
Evening.

153
00:09:39,083 --> 00:09:41,292
-Everything in order?
-Of course, Officer.

154
00:09:46,542 --> 00:09:49,124
We're done here. Take these guys away.
Get 'em in the truck.

155
00:09:49,125 --> 00:09:51,250
How's it going, Officer? Need any help?

156
00:09:51,833 --> 00:09:55,332
Oh, no, we'll be okay.
As you can see, I've got it under control.

157
00:09:55,333 --> 00:09:57,375
-Excuse me.
-Hurry up.

158
00:10:06,750 --> 00:10:07,833
All right, on your feet.

159
00:10:10,583 --> 00:10:12,832
All right, asshole, show me some ID.

160
00:10:12,833 --> 00:10:16,792
-We just got here from Tijuana yesterday.
-Yeah, this <i>pendejo.</i>

161
00:10:18,750 --> 00:10:19,750
MUNICIPAL POLICE

162
00:10:25,917 --> 00:10:27,792
Hey, I'm keeping my eye on you.

163
00:10:29,833 --> 00:10:31,792
All right, let's get the fuck out of here.

164
00:10:34,333 --> 00:10:37,417
I'm guessing you've already started
logging the evidence, right?

165
00:10:39,250 --> 00:10:40,375
Standard practice, Officer.

166
00:10:43,292 --> 00:10:45,583
-Hey, don't do...
-Don't do what?

167
00:10:46,500 --> 00:10:48,083
Know your place.

168
00:10:50,625 --> 00:10:52,083
That's a lot of coke.

169
00:10:53,583 --> 00:10:57,000
Just say the word and we'd be happy
to provide an escort to the DA.

170
00:10:59,875 --> 00:11:02,917
Or actually, I should probably
just call in the seizure now.

171
00:11:14,417 --> 00:11:15,667
Okay, Officer.

172
00:11:17,750 --> 00:11:19,042
Let's go to Ahome.

173
00:11:19,917 --> 00:11:20,917
Come on.

174
00:11:24,333 --> 00:11:25,333
Hey!

175
00:11:31,792 --> 00:11:33,167
Can I help you, gentlemen?

176
00:11:34,042 --> 00:11:35,417
Is there a problem?

177
00:11:47,125 --> 00:11:48,125
I'm cool.

178
00:11:48,833 --> 00:11:50,042
Then move along.

179
00:12:14,417 --> 00:12:15,417
Lead the way.

180
00:12:18,375 --> 00:12:20,542
Come on, let's go! Let's move out!

181
00:12:32,375 --> 00:12:33,875
Dispatch, do you read?

182
00:12:34,458 --> 00:12:36,332
-Carmona...
-<i>This is dispatch.</i>

183
00:12:36,333 --> 00:12:38,792
Do you realize
you just screwed with that officer's deal?

184
00:12:44,750 --> 00:12:47,125
All right. Thanks, Erick.

185
00:12:55,833 --> 00:12:58,749
<i>I'll be waiting for you
at the motel, okay, baby?</i>

186
00:12:58,750 --> 00:13:00,333
<i>Save some energy for me.</i>

187
00:13:04,792 --> 00:13:05,833
Here you go.

188
00:13:11,875 --> 00:13:13,458
This is supposed to be good?

189
00:13:14,042 --> 00:13:16,208
Hm. It's the best in Mochis.

190
00:13:20,208 --> 00:13:21,833
Hey, Rosales.

191
00:13:23,042 --> 00:13:25,125
What was all that at the gas station?

192
00:13:29,292 --> 00:13:30,458
I'm sorry, what?

193
00:13:31,292 --> 00:13:33,833
What were you showing those assholes
on your phone?

194
00:13:35,042 --> 00:13:37,541
I'm a little confused
about how you do things.

195
00:13:37,542 --> 00:13:38,833
What the hell?

196
00:13:40,458 --> 00:13:43,042
Look, asshole, I don't have to explain
how I work to you.

197
00:13:47,667 --> 00:13:48,750
What's your problem?

198
00:13:51,292 --> 00:13:52,958
I don't have a problem.

199
00:14:03,667 --> 00:14:05,083
What a fucking prick.

200
00:14:15,917 --> 00:14:17,082
Arturo?

201
00:14:17,083 --> 00:14:17,999
Yeah.

202
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:19,124
Morning, honey.

203
00:14:19,125 --> 00:14:20,958
-Hey, good morning.
-I missed you.

204
00:14:21,875 --> 00:14:23,374
Want some breakfast? Are you hungry?

205
00:14:23,375 --> 00:14:26,082
I'm exhausted more than anything,
so I'll just eat whatever you have.

206
00:14:26,083 --> 00:14:29,417
There's <i>machaca.</i> And of course
you're tired. How could you not be?

207
00:14:31,625 --> 00:14:33,666
Wow, this is good. Who drew it?

208
00:14:33,667 --> 00:14:35,874
Joana. You know, the artist in the family.

209
00:14:35,875 --> 00:14:38,082
-She's pretty good.
-Here, have some juice too.

210
00:14:38,083 --> 00:14:39,250
Thank you.

211
00:14:40,958 --> 00:14:42,708
Okay, so how was it?

212
00:14:43,208 --> 00:14:46,250
How'd it go with your new partner?
What's he like?

213
00:14:49,708 --> 00:14:51,917
Well, I can't really figure out who he is.

214
00:14:52,500 --> 00:14:53,917
Why? What happened?

215
00:14:56,208 --> 00:14:58,416
I think it's first day-nerves
or something.

216
00:14:58,417 --> 00:14:59,417
Hm.

217
00:15:00,708 --> 00:15:01,708
How are you doing?

218
00:15:06,125 --> 00:15:07,125
Fine.

219
00:15:08,375 --> 00:15:09,375
Um...

220
00:15:12,083 --> 00:15:16,042
Well, actually, I've been thinking
about what you said.

221
00:15:16,917 --> 00:15:18,666
-And I think that maybe...
-Wait.

222
00:15:18,667 --> 00:15:21,041
-I was just...
-I'm sorry.

223
00:15:21,042 --> 00:15:24,083
To be honest, I was caught off guard.

224
00:15:26,500 --> 00:15:29,060
But one more kid isn't that different,
so I'm sure we'll be okay.

225
00:15:31,500 --> 00:15:32,542
You sure?

226
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:38,375
Completely sure.

227
00:16:15,917 --> 00:16:18,417
Honey, are you okay?

228
00:16:20,042 --> 00:16:21,042
What time is it?

229
00:16:22,375 --> 00:16:24,249
It's a little after seven o'clock.

230
00:16:24,250 --> 00:16:27,500
Your partner was early,
so I let him inside. He's on the couch.

231
00:16:30,708 --> 00:16:31,917
Rosales?

232
00:16:45,708 --> 00:16:46,875
Hey, girls?

233
00:16:49,333 --> 00:16:51,792
-You girls do your homework?
-Yes, Papa.

234
00:16:52,500 --> 00:16:53,791
Wow, I'm proud of both of you.

235
00:16:53,792 --> 00:16:56,666
Now go to your rooms
and get ready for bed. Come on.

236
00:16:56,667 --> 00:16:59,124
-Nice to meet you. And be careful tonight.
-Have a good night.

237
00:16:59,125 --> 00:17:00,624
-I got it.
-Thanks.

238
00:17:00,625 --> 00:17:02,458
Come on, girls. Brush your teeth.

239
00:17:03,750 --> 00:17:04,875
Why are you so early?

240
00:17:05,458 --> 00:17:07,750
I, uh... I, uh, got you a peace offering.

241
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:18,792
Give me ten. I'll be right out.

242
00:17:20,417 --> 00:17:22,000
You have a beautiful family.

243
00:17:37,750 --> 00:17:39,750
You know, when I got assigned
to work with you,

244
00:17:40,667 --> 00:17:42,250
you sounded familiar.

245
00:17:43,500 --> 00:17:46,000
But I really couldn't figure out
from where though.

246
